## Conversation
While watching the first-ever full-CI run on PR #14965 (head 3c74eeb86), the `dynamo-runtime / mypy` job failed with 12 errors in components/src/dynamo/vllm/mooncake_store_runtime.py. User had asked to watch CI and then plan a stacked-PR split; this fix was needed first.

## Actions
Reproduced with `MYPYPATH=components/src:lib/bindings/python/src mypy --explicit-package-bases components/src/dynamo/vllm` after `uv pip install mypy==1.18.2` into .venv (pin from container/deps/requirements.test.txt). Fixed: `vllm.__file__` Optional narrowing via explicit raise; `seen: set[int]`; `projection: list[int | None]`; `groups: list[dict[str, Any]]`; `main`/`result` narrowing via explicit `if x is None: raise UnsupportedContract(...)` instead of `_require` (which is not a TypeGuard so mypy cannot narrow through it); class-level `vllm_config: Any` on the mixin. 59 Mooncake Python tests still pass; pre-commit on the file clean.

## Errors & Mistakes
None.

## Dead Ends
Considered making `_require` a TypeGuard; not expressible for arbitrary boolean conditions. Considered `assert x is not None`; asserts can be stripped and the repo raises UnsupportedContract elsewhere, so an explicit raise is the behavior-preserving choice.

## Hints for Future Agents
- Pre-merge (pre-merge.yml) does not run mypy. Only the full `PR` workflow's `dynamo-runtime / mypy` job does, so new Python modules can sit unchecked until the first `/ok to test`. Run the CI invocation above locally before requesting full CI.
- The remaining local mypy error (`yaml` stubs in omni/stage_worker.py) is a missing `types-PyYAML` in .venv, present on main, and not a CI failure.
- `test_vllm_unit.py` cannot be collected without `vllm` installed; the three Mooncake test files can.

